{"cut_proposal":{"candidate_errors":[],"prefix":"To solve the problem, we need to determine the possible values of \\( n \\) such that \\( n + 2005 \\) has exactly 21 positive factors. We start by analyzing the factorization of 21. The number 21 can be factored into positive integers in the following ways:\n\\[ 21 = 21 \\times 1 \\]\n\\[ 21 = 7 \\times 3 \\]\n\nThis means the number \\( n + 2005 \\) must be of the form \\( p^{20} \\) or \\( p_1^2 p_2^2 \\), where \\( p \\) and \\( p_1, p_2 \\) are prime numbers.\n\n### Case 1: \\( n + 2005 = p^{20} \\)\nWe need to find a prime number \\( p \\) such that \\( p^{20} - 2005 \\) is a positive integer less than 10,000. We check the smallest primes:\n- For \\( p = 2 \\):\n  \\[ 2^{20} = 1048576 \\]\n  \\[ 2^{20} - 2005 = 1048576 - 2005 = 1046571 \\]\n  This is greater than 10,000, so \\( p = 2 \\) is not a solution.\n- For \\( p = 3 \\):\n  \\[ 3^{20} = 3486784401 \\]\n  This is much greater than 10,000, so \\( p = 3 \\) is not a solution.\n- For \\( p = 5 \\):\n  \\[ 5^{20} = 95367431640625 \\]\n  This is much greater than 10,000, so \\( p = 5 \\) is not a solution.\n\nSince \\( p^{20} \\) grows very quickly, there are no solutions for \\( p \\geq 2 \\). Therefore, there are no solutions in this case.\n\n","prefix_end":1149,"status":"review_required"},"eligible":true,"generation":{"generation":{"max_new_tokens":2048,"temperature":0.7,"top_k":0,"top_p":1.0},"ids":[1249,11625,279,3491,11,582,1184,311,8253,279,3204,2750,315,17767,308,1124,8,1741,429,17767,308,488,220,17,15,15,20,1124,8,702,6896,220,17,16,6785,9363,13,1205,1191,553,41018,279,8168,2022,315,220,17,16,13,576,1372,220,17,16,646,387,2097,3018,1119,6785,25780,304,279,2701,5510,510,78045,220,17,16,284,220,17,16,1124,15136,220,16,1124,921,78045,220,17,16,284,220,22,1124,15136,220,18,1124,2533,1986,3363,279,1372,17767,308,488,220,17,15,15,20,1124,8,1969,387,315,279,1352,17767,281,47822,17,15,92,1124,8,476,17767,281,62,16,61,17,281,62,17,61,17,1124,701,1380,17767,281,